From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Clint Goudie-Nice <clint-goudie-nice@example.net>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 12:30:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] l2mcd_cli: hold a dump line to its buffer

l2mcd_ctl's dumps build each line in the 4000-byte pbuf with

    j += snprintf(pbuf + j, L2MCD_PBUF_SIZE - j, ...);

snprintf() returns the length it would have written, not what fitted. A
line longer than the buffer therefore takes j past its end, and the next
call's size, L2MCD_PBUF_SIZE - j, is negative: converted to size_t it is
no bound at all, and the call writes at pbuf + j, past the buffer, for as
long as the dump has entries. The fortified build does not catch it:
__snprintf_chk() is given an unknown object size for pbuf + j.

The lines that can get there: a VLAN's port list (-c 5) from about 333
entries, its member tree (-c 12) from about 210 members, a port's VLANs
(-c 6) from about 800 VLANs, a VLAN's addresses (-c 9). The group dump
stopped at the end already, and the static group's line wrote up to 25
bytes from as far as 21 bytes before the end.

Every append goes through pbuf_append() now, which writes nothing once
the line is full; a line that does not fit is printed cut.

The harness's cli-long-port-list case (a VLAN's port list with 402
entries) and cli-long-vlan-bitmap (a port in 4094 VLANs) run past pbuf
without this (UBSan: index 4008, and 4003, out of bounds for type
'char[4000]').
---
 port/l2mcd_cli.c | 44 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++------------
 1 file changed, 32 insertions(+), 12 deletions(-)

diff --git a/port/l2mcd_cli.c b/port/l2mcd_cli.c
index 5110da5..439bbf9 100644
--- a/port/l2mcd_cli.c
+++ b/port/l2mcd_cli.c
@@ -16,6 +16,7 @@
  */
 
 #include <sys/types.h>
+#include <stdarg.h>
 #include "l2mcd.h"
 #include <linux/filter.h>
 #include "mld_vlan_db.h"
@@ -31,6 +32,25 @@ extern struct list *snooping_enabled_vlans[MCAST_AFI_MAX];
 #define L2MCD_PBUF_SIZE 4000
 char pbuf[L2MCD_PBUF_SIZE];
 
+/* Append to the line in pbuf at *j. snprintf() returns the length it would
+ * have written, so a line longer than pbuf took j past its end, and the next
+ * call's size, L2MCD_PBUF_SIZE - j, was negative: as a size_t no bound at all,
+ * written at pbuf + j. A full line takes nothing more and is printed cut. */
+static void pbuf_append(int *j, const char *fmt, ...) __attribute__((format(printf, 2, 3)));
+static void pbuf_append(int *j, const char *fmt, ...)
+{
+    va_list ap;
+    int n;
+
+    if (*j < 0 || *j >= L2MCD_PBUF_SIZE - 1)
+        return;
+    va_start(ap, fmt);
+    n = vsnprintf(pbuf + *j, L2MCD_PBUF_SIZE - *j, fmt, ap);
+    va_end(ap);
+    if (n > 0)
+        *j = (n < L2MCD_PBUF_SIZE - *j) ? *j + n : L2MCD_PBUF_SIZE - 1;
+}
+
